{"DocComment":" [`write()`] and [`format()`] functions can be safely performed."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" You can use the `Arguments<'a>` that [`format_args!`] returns in `Debug`"},{"DocComment":" and `Display` contexts as seen below. The example also shows that `Debug`"},{"DocComment":" and `Display` format to the same thing: the interpolated format string"},{"DocComment":" in `format_args!`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```rust"},{"DocComment":" let debug = format!(\"{:?}\", format_args!(\"{} foo {:?}\", 1, 2));"},{"DocComment":" let display = format!(\"{}\", format_args!(\"{} foo {:?}\", 1, 2));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(\"1 foo 2\", display);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(display, debug);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`format()`]: ../../std/fmt/fn.format.html"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"FormatArguments","diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":"'a","variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Shared"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"src":"Normal","kind":"Opaque","layout":[{"key":"x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu","value":{"size":{"chosen":{"Deduplicated":91},"guarantee":null},"align":{"chosen":{"Deduplicated":89},"guarantee":null},"discriminator":{"Known":0},"inhabited":{"Deduplicated":0},"variant_layouts":[{"field_offsets":[{"guarantee":null,"chosen":0},{"guarantee":null,"chosen":8}],"inhabited":{"Deduplicated":0},"tagger":[]}],"repr":{"repr_algo":"Rust","align_modif":null,"transparent":false,"explicit_discr_type":null}}}],"ptr_metadata":"None","marker_traits":null},{"def_id":29,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["ops",0]},{"Ident":["range",0]},{"Ident":["RangeFrom",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":8,"beg":{"line":202,"col":0},"end":{"line":202,"col":25}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" A range only bounded inclusively below (`start..`)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The `RangeFrom` `start..` contains all values with `x >= start`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" *Note*: Overflow in the [`Iterator`] implementation (when the contained"},{"DocComment":" data type reaches its numerical limit) is allowed to panic, wrap, or"},{"DocComment":" saturate. This behavior is defined by the implementation of the [`Step`]"},{"DocComment":" trait. For primitive integers, this follows the normal rules, and respects"},{"DocComment":" the overflow checks profile (panic in debug, wrap in release). Note also"},{"DocComment":" that overflow happens earlier than you might assume: the overflow happens"},{"DocComment":" in the call to `next` that yields the maximum value, as the range must be"},{"DocComment":" set to a state to yield the next value."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`Step`]: crate::iter::Step"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The `start..` syntax is a `RangeFrom`:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((2..), std::ops::RangeFrom { start: 2 });"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(2 + 3 + 4, (2..).take(3).sum());"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let arr = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4];"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(arr[ ..  ], [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(arr[ .. 3], [0, 1, 2      ]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(arr[ ..=3], [0, 1, 2, 3   ]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(arr[1..  ], [   1, 2, 3, 4]); // This is a `RangeFrom`"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(arr[1.. 3], [   1, 2      ]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(arr[1..=3], [   1, 2, 3   ]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"RangeFrom","diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"